defect_patch_text:
Proposed patch, not applied or runtime-validated. Own returned observer work in the existing session observer API; publish synchronously as today, and drain only AFTER native job/cleanup disposal, before postmortem.quit. Never register the Brain receipt promise as isolation cleanup: that would make the settled receipt depend on its own prerequisite.

1. Update observer callback return contracts at host src/extensibility/extensions/types.ts:443, runner.ts:458 and :622, AgentSession.observeAttemptSettlement, and adapter types/prime.d.ts:97 from `=> void` to `=> void | Promise<void>`. No snapshot payload/version or lifecycle sequence change is needed. The registry callback can remain void because the session wrapper below owns the returned work.

2. In src/session/agent-session.ts, replace the observer forwarding method and add the following session-owned drain. The map holds an observed attempt until its LAST terminal observation callback finishes. It also covers a cleanup observation arriving after the native manager's short drain deadline. Rejection or timeout never creates a receipt:

private readonly settlementObserverDrains = new Map<Promise<void>, () => AttemptSettlementSnapshot>();

observeAttemptSettlement(
  observer: (snapshot: AttemptSettlementSnapshot) => void | Promise<void>,
  options?: { sourceToolCallId?: string },
): (() => void) | undefined {
  const attempts = new Map<string, {
    snapshot: AttemptSettlementSnapshot;
    done: ReturnType<typeof Promise.withResolvers<void>>;
    work?: Promise<void>;
  }>();
  return AttemptSettlementRegistry.instance().observe(snapshot => {
    let entry = attempts.get(snapshot.attemptId);
    if (!entry) {
      entry = { snapshot, done: Promise.withResolvers<void>() };
      attempts.set(snapshot.attemptId, entry);
      const owned = entry;
      this.settlementObserverDrains.set(entry.done.promise, () => owned.snapshot);
    }
    entry.snapshot = snapshot;
    const owned = entry;
    let work: Promise<void>;
    try {
      work = Promise.resolve(observer(snapshot));
    } catch (error) {
      logger.warn("Attempt settlement observer threw", { attemptId: snapshot.attemptId, revision: snapshot.revision, error: String(error) });
      return; // Retain the unresolved drain; bounded teardown will report abandonment.
    }
    owned.work = work;
    void work.then(() => {
      if (owned.work !== work) return;
      if (!snapshot.releasePermitted && snapshot.cleanupState !== "failed") return;
      attempts.delete(snapshot.attemptId);
      this.settlementObserverDrains.delete(owned.done.promise);
      owned.done.resolve();
    }, error => {
      logger.warn("Attempt settlement observer rejected", { attemptId: snapshot.attemptId, revision: snapshot.revision, error: String(error) });
      // Keep this attempt visible to the bounded abandonment report.
    });
  }, options);
}

private async drainSettlementObservers(): Promise<void> {
  if (this.settlementObserverDrains.size === 0) return;
  logger.debug("Attempt settlement observer drain started", { pending: this.settlementObserverDrains.size });
  try {
    await withTimeout((async () => {
      while (this.settlementObserverDrains.size > 0) {
        await Promise.all([...this.settlementObserverDrains.keys()]);
      }
    })(), 30_000, "Attempt settlement observer drain timed out");
    logger.debug("Attempt settlement observer drain completed");
  } catch (error) {
    for (const current of this.settlementObserverDrains.values()) {
      const snapshot = current();
      logger.warn("Attempt settlement observation abandoned at teardown", {
        attemptId: snapshot.attemptId,
        agentId: snapshot.agentId,
        revision: snapshot.revision,
        cleanupState: snapshot.cleanupState,
        releasePermitted: snapshot.releasePermitted,
        reason: String(error),
      });
    }
    // No synthetic acknowledgement, release, or completion.
  }
}

Call `await this.drainSettlementObservers();` in #doDispose AFTER the Promise.allSettled teardown block and its rejected-result logging (currently around 4915), before closing session resources. Do NOT call it from the early session_shutdown event or inside #disposeOwnedAsyncJobs before native cleanup starts. This bounds waiting without delaying settlement publication. A terminal callback returning false is an explicit refusal, not an acceptance; its diagnostics below must say so.

